---
// "Why this hour": one big statement. The middle sentence fades in grey.
---

<section class="statement">
  <div class="shell">
    <p class="statement__text" data-reveal>
      Barriers in triathlon rarely announce themselves.
      <span class="statement__muted">
        A training session nobody with kids can make. A committee where everyone looks the
        same. A race kit that only comes in one cut.
      </span>
      Our speakers ran into these and kept going.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .statement {
    background: var(--paper);
    color: var(--ink);
    padding-block: clamp(80px, 10vw, 136px);
  }

  .statement__text {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 24ch;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.6vw, 3.1rem);
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .statement__muted {
    color: rgba(24, 24, 26, 0.4);
  }
</style>
